{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>They are known</b> — Rabbi Moses said: this is connected with the verse after it, and it describes that at the time when they were building the house of YHWH, and the hewers were hewing the stones, the one bringing axes into the thicket to hew stone would be reckoned as bringing them upward, for he reached a higher level, and thus it is 'known above' — like one bringing axes into a thicket of trees. And in my opinion: at the time when the axes are brought into a thicket of trees, to cut the wood that was for the building of the house, there was a din above."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {0 "The comment addresses Psalms 74:5 but invokes the building of the Temple; the Hebrew is syntactically difficult throughout, and I have translated hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:25.583683776Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}